            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h4><strong>What Makes Smart Air Purifiers Cost More Than Basic Models</strong></h4><p>Anyone shopping for an air purifier sees the same problem: prices jump when you add smart features. A basic purifier might cost $100. Add WiFi, sensors, and app control, and you are looking at $300 to $600. The question is simple: does the extra money actually get you something useful?</p><p>Not every smart feature matters. Some genuinely improve your life. Others sound impressive but do nothing practical. This guide shows which features solve real problems and which ones just look good on the marketing materials.</p><h4><strong>Does Advanced Filtration Actually Work Better Than Basic HEPA</strong></h4>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_Xi6zz4": {
